            text: `<p></p> <p>The <i>iterated logarithm</i> of a number  \\(  n  \\), denoted by  \\(  \\log^{*} n  \\), is defined as the minimum number of successive applications of the base-2 logarithm required to reduce the value to at most 1.<br><br>Formally,  \$\$  \\log^{*} n = \\min \\left\\{ k \\,\\middle|\\, \\underbrace{\\log \\log \\cdots \\log}_{k\\ \\text{times}} n \\le 1 \\right\\}.  \$\$ Examples:  \$\$  \\log^{*} 2 = 1,\\quad \\log^{*} 4 = 2,\\quad \\log^{*} 16 = 3,\\quad \\log^{*} 65536 = 4,\\quad \\log^{*}(2^{65536}) = 5.  \$\$ <br><br>Assume that <code>log()</code> computes the base-2 logarithm.<br><br>Which of the following correctly represent or implement  \\(  \\log^{*} n  \\)? </p> <table cellpadding="12" style="width:100%; border-collapse:collapse; text-align:left; border-spacing: 0px;"> <tbody> <tr> <td style="border:1px solid #ccc; vertical-align:top; width:50%;"><b>A.</b> <pre>int iteratedLog(double n)
{
    if (n &gt; 1.0) {
        return 1 + iteratedLog(log(n));
    }
    return 0;
}
</pre> </td> <td style="border:1px solid #ccc; vertical-align:top; width:50%;"><b>B.</b> <pre>int iteratedLog(double n)
{
    int count = 0;
    while (n &gt; 1.0) {
        n = log(n);
        count++;
    }
    return count;
}
</pre> </td> </tr> <tr> <td style="border:1px solid #ccc; vertical-align:top;"><b>C.</b><br> \$\$  \\log^{*} n = \\begin{cases} 0, &amp; n \\le 1, \\\\[4pt] 1 + \\log^{*}(\\log n), &amp; n &gt; 1. \\end{cases}  \$\$ </td> <td style="border:1px solid #ccc; vertical-align:top;"><b>D.</b><br> \\( \\log ^*\\left(2^m\\right)= \\begin{cases} 1+\\log ^*(m) &amp; \\text{ if } m&gt;1 \\\\ 0 &amp; \\text{ if } m \\leq 0 \\\\ 1 &amp; \\text{ if } 0&lt;m \\leq 1 \\end{cases} \\) </td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p></p>`,
