            text: `<p></p> <p>Consider the following set of relations:</p> <p> \\( \\text{EMP}(\\underline{\\textsf{eno}}, \\textsf{ename, dno)} \\)<br> \\( \\textsf{DEPT}( \\underline{\\textsf{dno}}, \\textsf{dname)} \\) </p> <p>Primary key columns are underlined and  \\( \\textsf{dno} \\) in  \\( \\textsf{EMP} \\) is a foreign key referring primary key of  \\( \\textsf{DEPT} \\) table.<br>Now consider the following queries: </p> <p> \\( \\textbf{QUERY : 1} \\) </p> <pre class="prettyprint linenums lang-sql prettyprinted" data-pbcklang="sql" data-pbcktabsize="4" style=""><ol class="linenums"><li class="L0"><span class="pln">SELECT </span><span class="pun">*</span><span class="pln"> </span></li><li class="L1"><span class="pln">FROM emp e</span><span class="pun">,</span><span class="pln"> dept d</span></li><li class="L2"><span class="pln">WHERE e</span><span class="pun">.</span><span class="pln">dno </span><span class="pun">=</span><span class="pln"> d</span><span class="pun">.</span><span class="pln">dno</span><span class="pun">;</span></li></ol></pre> <p> \\( \\textbf{QUERY : 2} \\) </p> <pre class="prettyprint linenums lang-sql prettyprinted" data-pbcklang="sql" data-pbcktabsize="4" style=""><ol class="linenums"><li class="L0"><span class="pln">SELECT </span><span class="pun">*</span><span class="pln"> </span></li><li class="L1"><span class="pln">FROM emp NATURAL JOIN dept</span><span class="pun">;</span></li></ol></pre> <p>Then which of the following statements are TRUE regarding the above queries?</p> <ol style="list-style-type:upper-roman"> <li>Both Query  \\( :1 \\) and Query  \\( :2 \\) returns same no of rows. </li> <li>Both Query  \\( :1 \\) and Query  \\( :2 \\) returns same no of columns. </li> <li>Both Query  \\( : 1 \\) and Query  \\( :2 \\) returns different no of rows. </li> <li>Both Query  \\( :1 \\) and Query  \\( :2 \\) returns different no of columns. </li> </ol> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p></p>`,
